From 2270de906cd3120b108973bcce82c89830af0287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:18:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] perf(sim): B2 G2 services, NIMBY, police need: one
 method per piece kind (R10)

Every services sub-state's loop moves out of its dispatcher's switch into a
method of its own or a module function over typed arrays (sumRange,
countRoads, clampRange, tierStatsRange, composeRange, the access / shop
row loops, comboRange, finishStatsRange, staleRange); the tier engine's
items (init, search, alloc, report, the final items) and NimbyRun's and
PoliceNeedRun's stages likewise. The footprint max reads the multi-cell
lots as typed rects (lotMaxRange), not Buildings, and the stats
accumulators and the lot scratch are fields reset at every pass start, so
no scratch value depends on the piece size.

Results are unchanged: b2PiecesServices, the NIMBY exactness test and the
WASM tier engine sections pass as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
